# Keep model weights OUT of Docker build contexts.
#
# Weights belong in a volume-mounted HuggingFace cache, never baked into an
# image.  These patterns exist so that `docker build` never accidentally ships
# hundreds of GB of checkpoints even if a Dockerfile author forgets to scope
# their COPY lines.  Adding a new directory that could hold weights?  Add it
# here too.

# HuggingFace / transformers caches (if anyone symlinks them into the repo)
.cache/
**/.cache/huggingface/
**/.cache/torch/
**/.cache/jax/
**/__pycache__/

# Weight file types — any COPY . or COPY ./* would otherwise pick these up.
**/*.gguf
**/*.safetensors
**/*.bin
**/*.pth
**/*.pt
**/*.ckpt
**/*.onnx
**/*.tflite
**/*.h5
**/*.msgpack
**/*.flax

# Local snapshot / downloaded checkpoint dirs used by experiments
results/*_weights/
results/*_checkpoint/
results/*_model/
results/*.safetensors
models/
checkpoints/

# Python build / env artefacts that inflate build context for no reason
.venv/
venv/
env/
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Rust build artefacts — the webgpu-gateway Dockerfile uses a multi-stage
# build but keeping target/ out of the initial context still speeds things up.
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# Secrets — never ship these
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*_rsa
*_ed25519

# Local state the conductor writes
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
/tmp/conductor.log
